{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TheGiddyLimit/5etools-utils/master/schema/brew-fast/homebrew.json",
  "subclass": [
    {
      "name": "Judge of Limbo",
      "source": "ECDC-Nerav",
      "className": "Warlock",
      "classSource": "PHB",
      "shortName": "Limbo",
      "additionalSpells": [
        {
          "expanded": {
            "1": ["cure wounds", "inflict wounds"],
            "3": ["lesser restoration", "gentle repose"],
            "5": ["animate dead", "feign death"],
            "7": ["death ward", "spirit of death"],
            "9": ["greater restoration", "raise dead"]
          }
        }
      ],
      "subclassFeatures": [
        "A Delicate Balance|Warlock|PHB|Limbo|ECDC-Nerav|1",
        "Expanded Spell List|Warlock|PHB|Limbo|ECDC-Nerav|1",
        "Unnatural Body|Warlock|PHB|Limbo|ECDC-Nerav|6",
        "Perpetuity|Warlock|PHB|Limbo|ECDC-Nerav|10",
        "Borrowed Life|Warlock|PHB|Limbo|ECDC-Nerav|14"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "subclassFeature": [
    {
      "name": "A Delicate Balance",
      "source": "ECDC-Nerav",
      "level": 1,
      "className": "Warlock",
      "classSource": "PHB",
      "subclassShortName": "Limbo",
      "subclassSource": "ECDC-Nerav",
      "entries": [
        "Starting level 1 you learn the {@spell Spare the Dying} cantrip, which counts as a warlock cantrip. You also have advantage against any sickness related spell",
        "Additionally, if any other creature that you can see within 30 feet would have their hp fall below 0 or less, you can use your reaction to transfer up to {@dice 1d4} + your Constitution modifier Hit Points to them. Once you use this effect, you cannot use it again until you finish a long rest."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Expanded Spell List",
      "source": "ECDC-Nerav",
      "level": 1,
      "className": "Warlock",
      "classSource": "PHB",
      "subclassShortName": "Limbo",
      "subclassSource": "ECDC-Nerav",
      "entries": [
        "The Judge of Limbo allows you to learn new Warlock spells.",
        "The following list is addd to the spells that you can learn:",
        {
          "type": "table",
          "caption": "Expanded Spell List",
          "colLabels": ["Warlock Level", "Spell"],
          "colStyles": ["col-2 text-center", "col-10"],
          "rows": [
            ["1st", "{@spell Cure Wounds}, {@spell Inflict Wounds}"],
            ["3rd", "{@spell Lesser Restoration}, {@spell Gentle repose}"],
            ["5th", "{@spell Animate Dead}, {@spell Feign Death}"],
            ["7th", "{@spell Death Ward}, {@spell Spirit of Death}"],
            ["9th", "{@spell Greater Restoration}, {@spell Raise Dead}"]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Unnatural Body",
      "source": "ECDC-Nerav",
      "className": "Warlock",
      "classSource": "PHB",
      "subclassShortName": "Limbo",
      "subclassSource": "ECDC-Nerav",
      "level": 6,
      "entries": [
        "Starting level 6, your body commences to slow down it's metabolis. You gain poison resistance and you only require 4 hours to benefit from a long rest."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Perpetuity",
      "source": "ECDC-Nerav",
      "className": "Warlock",
      "classSource": "PHB",
      "subclassShortName": "Limbo",
      "subclassSource": "ECDC-Nerav",
      "level": 10,
      "entries": [
        "Starting your 10th level, you can keep your breath indefinetely, you don't require food, water or sleep. Althought to benefit from rests you still need to perform them.",
        "You age slowly. Every 10 years your body only ages 1, additionaly you are immune to being magically aged."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Borrowed Life",
      "source": "ECDC-Nerav",
      "className": "Warlock",
      "classSource": "PHB",
      "subclassShortName": "Limbo",
      "subclassSource": "ECDC-Nerav",
      "level": 14,
      "entries": [
        "When you reach 14th level, your body gains accelerated regenerative capacities. On combat during yoiur turn you can use your bonus action to recover {@dice 1d8} + your Warlock level Hit points. Additionally you can use this feature to re-attach lost body parts without any inconvenient.",
        "Once you use this feature, you cannot use it again until the next short or long rest."
      ]
    }
  ],
